{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Face milling of 42CrMo4: surface roughness and spindle power",
  "notes": "Face milling of quenched and tempered 42CrMo4 (approx. 300 HB) blocks on a 5-axis machining centre with a Ø50 mm face mill, 4 coated carbide inserts, emulsion coolant. Each run machines one 200 mm long pass. Flank wear VB of the leading insert is measured with a tool microscope before each run and recorded as an environmental factor; the insert set is replaced when VB exceeds 0.25 mm (see run notes). Ra is the mean of three profilometer traces across the feed marks (λc = 0.8 mm); spindle power is the mean cutting power from the spindle drive minus the idle power at the same speed.",
  "factors": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "symbol": "A",
      "name": "Cutting speed",
      "units": "m/min",
      "kind": {
        "type": "continuous",
        "low": 150.0,
        "high": 250.0
      },
      "role": "controlled"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "symbol": "B",
      "name": "Feed per tooth",
      "units": "mm",
      "kind": {
